  "video": {
    "@type": "VideoObject",
    "contentUrl": "https://content.jwplatform.com/videos/5ZogZy8T-K3AjnAEN.mp4",
    "description": "With a texture approximating pizza dough, this delicious flatbread begins with a mixture of bread flour, active dry yeast, sugar and warm water. After an hour of fermenting, add kosher salt, olive oil and more bread flour until you have a sticky ball of dough! Knead the dough until elastic, then let rise coated in olive oil until doubled, then chill overnight. Roll dough thin, then press thin onto an upside down bowl. Transfer to a super-hot cast iron pan and cook! Thinner and stretchier than pita, you’ll love this flatbread!",
